# civic-data .gitignore — the decided GitHub shape (TODO.md "Publish to GitHub"):
# commit the TEXT layer (markdown, CSVs, JSON, per-city SQLite dbs, weeks/, scripts,
# docs); keep bulky re-fetchable binaries, oversized derived artifacts, and secrets
# local-only.

# raw originals at ANY depth (PDF/video/audio/images) — public + re-fetchable via
# each index.csv source_url / sources.csv; several exceed GitHub's 100 MB hard limit.
# NOTE: raw TEXT artifacts live in <dataset>/text/ (committed), not raw/.
raw/

# slc public_comments predates the raw/ convention: its year folders hold the weekly
# comment source PDFs (221 files, 364 MB) — same raw-stays-local policy.
slc_city_council/public_comments/20*/*.pdf

# QC source packets retained for comment ground-truthing (re-fetchable; 43 MB files)
_audits/comment_qc/**/*.pdf

# SLCo even-year canonical long file (78 MB — over GitHub's 50 MB warning): DERIVED,
# regenerates in ~2 min from the mirrored raws via
# salt_lake_county/elections/normalize_sovc_county.py (gate-verified); the committed
# county_results_by_contest.csv + county_races.csv are the federated/audited layers.
salt_lake_county/elections/slco_county_results_long.csv

# gov.db is DERIVED (1.64 GB — 16x over GitHub's 100 MB hard limit) — regenerate with
# `python3 scripts/build_cities_db.py` (runs the search layer too), or download the
# release asset (gov.db.gz, ~399 MiB). The per-entity db/*.db files ARE committed
# (small, and the federated build reads them). cities.db is its back-compat SYMLINK
# (renamed 2026-07-20) — also excluded, else clones get a dangling link.
/gov.db
/cities.db
/gov.db.tmp
/gov.db.lock

# ONE pathological packet-text sidecar: 110 MB of whitespace-bloat layout-mode
# extraction holding only ~37k words (over GitHub's hard limit). Content is
# re-derivable from the retained raw packet (see draper packets/index.csv);
# re-extraction lead filed in LEADS.md. Excluded 2026-07-31 (PUBLISH GATE G1).
draper_city_council/packets/text/2020-05-28_PlanningCommission_item1820_att1624.txt

# mag_mpo keeps its source PDFs under raw_pdf/ (name referenced by its
# minutes_index.csv + provenance headers, so not renamed to raw/) — same
# raw-stays-local policy as the 358 raw/ dirs.
mag_mpo/legislative/raw_pdf/

# scratch/backup dirs outside the _backups/ convention + stray editor backups
*/pmn_backfill/work/
_backup_*/
*.bak

# pre-change backups (local safety net, ~GBs)
_backups/

# local harness state (permission grants etc.)
.claude/settings.local.json

# secrets — per-dataset .env files carry ANTHROPIC_API_KEY
.env
*/.env
*/*/.env

# OS/tooling noise
.DS_Store
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Presentation copies of raw campaign-finance filings (interface_prototype/examples/).
# These are duplicates of gitignored raw/ originals and carry donor street addresses on
# the face of the filing — PRIVACY.md keeps unredacted source PDFs local-only. Local
# demo use is fine; publishing them is not.
interface_prototype/examples/campaign_finance/*.pdf
